{"sounds":{"intro":"Vietnamese uses the Latin alphabet with many accent marks. It has six tones in the north (the south merges some). The mark shows the tone: ma (mid), má (rising), mà (low falling), mả (dipping), mã (broken rising), mạ (low heavy). The same letters with a different tone are different words. Words are short and never change form.","rows":[["đ","like a hard English \"d\"","đi"],["d","\"y\" in the north, \"z\" in the north-west, \"y\" in the south","dạ"],["gi","like \"z\" in the north","giá"],["x","like \"s\"","xin"],["ch","like \"ch\", at the end of a word like \"k\"","chào"],["ng / ngh","like \"ng\" in \"singer\", also at the start of a word","nghe"],["nh","like \"ny\" in \"canyon\"","nhà"],["ă","short \"a\", like \"u\" in \"cut\"","ăn"],["â","short \"uh\" sound","cân"],["ơ","long \"uh\" sound, like \"ur\" in \"fur\"","cơm"],["ư","\"oo\" with spread lips","tư"]],"notes":["Tones matter more than anything else. \"Ma\" (ghost), \"má\" (mother or cheek), \"mà\" (but), \"mả\" (tomb), \"mã\" (horse), \"mạ\" (rice seedling).","Politeness is built into the pronouns. Choose by age: anh (older man), chị (older woman), em (younger person), ông (old man), bà (old woman), bạn (friend of the same age)."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","không","KHOHM"],["one","một","MOHT"],["two","hai","HIE"],["three","ba","BAH"],["four","bốn","BOHN"],["five","năm","NAHM"],["six","sáu","SOW"],["seven","bảy","BIE"],["eight","tám","TAHM"],["nine","chín","CHEEN"],["ten","mười","MWOY"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","mười một","mwoy MOHT"],["twelve","mười hai","mwoy HIE"],["thirteen","mười ba","mwoy BAH"],["fourteen","mười bốn","mwoy BOHN"],["fifteen","mười lăm","mwoy LAHM"],["sixteen","mười sáu","mwoy SOW"],["seventeen","mười bảy","mwoy BIE"],["eighteen","mười tám","mwoy TAHM"],["nineteen","mười chín","mwoy CHEEN"],["twenty","hai mươi","hie MWOY"]]},{"id":"tens-and-big-numbers","title":"Tens and big numbers","items":[["twenty-